<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 13.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 13.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	   346.03   2.18</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	   223.02   3.10</p>
<p> 3   Countrywide-PP	183.87   1.14</p>
<p> 4   Mayne Nickless	175.06   7.93</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	 124.04   2.27</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement    123.19   1.70</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold     82.80   2.31</p>
<p> 8   Westral Forest	 81.16   2.24</p>
<p> 9   Herald Rsc	     79.65   0.90</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	  78.42   1.09</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    2.00   0.87</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   3.46   0.84</p>
<p> 3   Premier Inv	     4.62   0.82</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd	     6.59   0.78</p>
<p> 5   BTR Plc		   6.66   6.20</p>
<p> 6   OLS Asia Hldgs	  7.06   0.84</p>
<p> 7   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.12   1.30</p>
<p> 8   Renison Goldflds	7.56   5.21</p>
<p> 9   FAI Life ltd	    7.86   0.81</p>
<p>10   Capcount Prop	   7.87   0.86</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
